  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-codex",
      "text": "A drop-in [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) extension that gives GPT models a Codex-style environment using the native, non-Code-Mode OpenAI Codex tool surface.\n\nLooking to run DeepSeek V4 Flash in Codex instead? See [dsv4-codex-proxy](https://github.com/ryanzhou/dsv4-codex-proxy).\n\nIt adds a **Codex-style mode** agent preset with:"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-codex",
      "text": "- grammar-constrained OpenAI custom tool calls for `apply_patch`;\n- Codex-shaped `exec_command`/`write_stdin` unified exec with yielded background sessions and interactive PTY support;\n- native Web Bash rows and a Codex-style live-process-only background terminal list;\n- Codex-shaped `update_plan`, `request_user_input`, and `view_image` function tools;\n- `/plan` collaboration mode and `/goal` long-running work over DSH's native state, review, and continuation primitives;\n- the GPT-5.6 Sol Codex system prompt from the user-selected prompt archive;\n- DSH's existing sandbox, approval, todo, question, attachment, and tool-presentation behavior underneath the Codex-style wire format."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why",
      "text": "GPT-5.6 does not perform as well in DSH's default Standard mode because its post-training expects the prompts, tools, schemas, and result formats used by Codex. Recreating those conventions gives GPT models a familiar environment where their coding behavior feels more at home, while preserving DSH's native experience for DeepSeek models. This makes it practical to use DeepSeek and GPT models side by side in the same DSH installation without forcing either through an unfamiliar agent setup."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "Version 0.2.0 targets DSH 0.1.0-rc.6 and pi-ai 0.82.1. The extension uses small runtime bridges because those DSH versions do not expose grammar metadata or package-provided preset roots as public extension seams. Dependencies are pinned so an incompatible DSH upgrade fails installation instead of silently changing behavior."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "Grammar custom tools require a GPT-5+ pi-ai route whose model metadata enables `supportsOpenAIGrammarTools`, such as the built-in OpenAI, OpenAI Codex, Azure OpenAI Responses, GitHub Copilot, opencode, or Cloudflare AI Gateway routes. Unsupported routes receive pi-ai's normal function-tool fallback."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Install the bundle into every DSH profile where the preset should be available:\n\n~~~sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add @ryantzhou/dsh-codex\n~~~\n\nAfter the command completes, restart that DSH process and select **Codex-style mode** when creating a session.\n\nRemove it with the matching package spec:\n\n~~~sh\ndsh plugin --profile web remove @ryantzhou/dsh-codex\n~~~"
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "1. adds this package's immutable preset directory to the active preset registry;\n2. wraps each pi-ai provider once, immediately before dispatch, to attach the `apply_patch` Lark grammar;\n3. maps Codex unified exec sessions onto DSH's background-job and PTY primitives;\n4. shadows the generic Web tool/job views with Codex Bash rows and live background terminals;\n5. composes native DSH plan and goal lifecycles with Codex-compatible model guidance;\n6. removes the delegate schemas and their tool-specific guidance from Codex prompt assemblies."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "The Codex tools themselves delegate to DSH's existing `bash`/`pwsh`, `todo_write`, `ask_user_question`, and `read_image` tools. This keeps policy enforcement and UI behavior in their existing owners. `apply_patch` runs the bundled parser and applicator through the same sandboxed shell delegate."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "~~~sh\ncorepack pnpm install\ncorepack pnpm check\ncorepack pnpm test\ncorepack pnpm build\ncorepack pnpm pack\n~~~"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "Original code is MIT licensed. Codex-derived grammar and behavioral references retain OpenAI's Apache-2.0 notice. The archived GPT-5.6 prompt is not covered by this project's MIT license; its collector applies CC0 but does not warrant third-party rights. See `NOTICE` and `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES`."
    }
  ],
